# These are CONTENT-ADDRESSED bytes, not source files.
#
# Every document in this tree is identified by the sha256 of its exact bytes,
# and the test suite asserts three of those hashes against the values Model
# Studio published. Any line-ending normalisation -- on checkout, on a machine
# with a different core.autocrlf, or on the sanitized mirror -- would change
# those hashes and break the binding for reasons that would look like a
# producer error rather than a git setting.
#
# So nothing here is text as far as git is concerned.
* -text -diff
